# Clean Code Practices

## Naming
- camelCase for variables and functions.
- PascalCase for React components and types.
- Descriptive, no cryptic abbreviations.

## Function Design
- Single responsibility; keep ≤40 LOC.
- Pure where practical; side-effects isolated.
- Extract shared logic into `/hooks` or `/lib`.

## Component Design
- One component per file.
- Compose small components instead of large monoliths.
- Co-locate styles (Tailwind classes) and tests.

## Comments & Docs
- Only when intent is non-obvious.
- Use TSDoc for complex utilities and API types.
- Prefer self-explanatory code over comments.

## Error Handling
```typescript
try {
  const { data, error } = await supabase.from('patients').insert(values).single();
  if (error) throw error;
} catch (err) {
  console.error('Insert failed', err);
  toast.error('Could not save patient');
}
```

## Testing
- React Testing Library for UI.
- Jest mocks for Supabase and Google APIs.
- One test file per component or util.

# Recommended Folder Structure

```
/project-root
  ├─ app/                 # Next.js routes (App Router)
  ├─ components/          # Reusable UI grouped by feature
  ├─ hooks/               # Custom React hooks
  ├─ lib/                 # Supabase client, helpers, calendar SDK
  ├─ types/               # Global TypeScript interfaces/enums
  ├─ styles/              # Tailwind config & global CSS
  ├─ public/              # Static assets
  ├─ supabase/            # SQL migrations & seed scripts
  ├─ tests/               # Unit/integration tests
  └─ .cursor/             # Rule files (this file lives here)
```

# Additional Tips
- Use `index.ts` barrels for cleaner imports.
- Keep folder nesting shallow (max depth ≈ 3).
- Place feature-specific assets beside their component.
